# Identity Resources & Access

## Resource types

| Type | Role | Duende ApiResource / scopes? |
|------|------|------------------------------|
| `AnnotationServer` | One annotation SQL database; holds the grants | Yes — scopes `{Name}.Read\|Annotate\|Review` |
| `AnnotationContext` | Openable binding of Volume + AnnotationServer under a Connectome | Yes — same scopes; default context keeps today's client names |
| `Connectome` | Groups contexts, servers, and volumes; has a default context | No — not ApiFacing (avoids name collisions with default context) |
| `SegmentationService` | Segmentation backend | Yes — scopes `{Name}.User\|Access Manager` |
| `Group` | User grouping / grants | No — management only |
| `OrganizationalUnit` | Hierarchy / ownership | No — management only (`Administrator`) |

API-facing types: `Special.ResourceTypes.ApiFacing` (`AnnotationServer`, `AnnotationContext`, `SegmentationService`, in preference order). Resource stores must filter to these when building ApiResources/ApiScopes.

`Volume` / `VolumeMirror` are plain tables, not resources. They belong to a Connectome. Mirrors of one set are exact clones (clients may load-balance); a different build is a new Volume.

## Annotation context access

- Effective context permissions = grants on the context ∪ grants on its annotation server, with Read implied by Annotate or Review. Use `UserAnnotationContextPermissionsAsync`, `UserEffectiveResourcePermissionsAsync`, or `IsUserPermittedEffectiveAsync`; do not check context grant rows alone.
- New grants go on the annotation server (`GrantUserAnnotationContextFullAccessAsync` does this). Context grants remain for image-only contexts and as the legacy rollback path.
- `AnnotationServerCatalogSync` creates annotation servers from each context's VikingXML `VolumeToEndpoint`, ensures a Connectome parent, and sets `ConnectomeId` on server/volume; it never merges volumes or contexts.

## Names are unique per type, not globally

`IsResourceNameTaken` is scoped by `ResourceTypeId`. A **Group** and an **AnnotationContext** may share the same name (e.g. both `"Yiu"`).

When resolving permissions or token scopes **by name**:

- Prefer AnnotationServer, then AnnotationContext, then SegmentationService (`FindApiFacingResourceAsync`). An annotation server is usually named after the oldest context that uses it (e.g. both `"RC1"`).
- Never use bare `Resource.FirstOrDefault(r => r.Name == name)` for login / scope checks — the Group row often wins by lower Id

```csharp
// BAD — may return Group "Yiu"
await context.Resource.FirstOrDefaultAsync(r => r.Name == name);

// GOOD
await context.FindApiFacingResourceAsync(name);
```

## Grants vs site admin

- Explicit access: `GrantedUserPermissions` + `GrantedGroupPermissions` (via recursive group membership, including virtual Anonymous)
- Site role `Administrator` (`Special.Roles.Admin`) has full access; list/token helpers short-circuit via `UserResourcePermissionsByType` / `IsUserPermitted`
- OrgUnit `Administrator` manages children in the **management UI**; it does **not** by itself populate annotation OAuth scopes

## OAuth scopes

- Standard: `openid`, `profile`, `Viking.Annotation`
- Per annotation server: `{ServerName}.Read`, `{ServerName}.Annotate`, `{ServerName}.Review`
- Per annotation context (legacy name shape, still accepted): `{ContextName}.Read|Annotate|Review`, checked against the context's annotation server too
- Do not treat `Viking.Annotation` as a context named `Viking` when parsing `resource.permission` scopes

## Which process does what

| Process | Typical ports | Responsibility |
|---------|---------------|----------------|
| IdentityServerStandalone | `:5001` | Discovery, `/connect/token`, resource/client stores |
| WebManagement | `:4001` | MVC admin, MyAccess, `api/permissions/*` (cookie/bearer) |
| WebApi | `:6001` | `/Permissions/*` (introspection / anonymous username endpoints) |

MyAccess and management UIs should query `ApplicationDbContext` (or authenticated APIs) — never call WebApi `/Permissions/AccessibleAnnotationContexts` without a bearer token (returns `{}`).

## Client AllowedScopes

`IdentityServerVikingClientStore` must rebuild AllowedScopes from the live resource store. Do not permanently cache clients — new contexts would cause `invalid_scope` until restart.
